 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "This 32-patient canakinumab cohort of undifferentiated autoinflammatory disease (uAIDs) gives individual-level data (sex, onset and diagnosis ages, clinical features, treatment) for one patient carrying a TNFAIP3 variant: '| 26 | M | TNFAIP3 {c.1217A>T, p.E406V}'.",
 "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand (no supplementary section present). Scope: only Table 3 ID 26 carries a TNFAIP3 variant; the other 31 cohort patients (variants in other genes or none) are out of scope and counted in cohort_size_as_stated = 32. Label '26' is the paper's own Table 3 'ID' value, used verbatim (the paper refers to another patient as 'Pt 4' but never prints 'Pt 26'). n_patients_reported = 1 is counted from Table 3 (one row, and one Table 2 row, list TNFAIP3); the authors never state the number in words. Table 3 columns (patients as rows): ID | Gender | Results of NGS | Fever | Rash | Serosites | Arthritis | GI | Eye | Hydrocephalus | Sensorineural hearing loss | Laboratory activity | Onset age | Age at the time of diagnosis | Initial treatment (non-biologic) | Initial treatment (biologic drugs) | Outcome. '+' read as present. Table 3's notes define only drug/outcome abbreviations, not '-'; so the '-' cells for patient 26 (Rash, Serosites, GI, Eye, Hydrocephalus, Sensorineural hearing loss) are not reported, with no rows. Gender 'M' read as male: Table 3 has 13 M and 19 W, matching '13 (41%) boys and 19 (59%) girls'. Table 3 prints ages without units; years taken from Table 1 headers ('Onset age, years'; 'Age of the diagnosis, years') and consistent with Pt 4 ('at 1.5 years' in text vs 1.4 in Table 3). ISO values written as decimal years (P5.7Y, P14.7Y). 'Laboratory activity +' is recorded as a feature but not mapped to checklist 'elevated inflammatory markers (CRP/ESR)', because the paper's 'laboratory activity' also covers WBC, platelets and hemoglobin. 'Fever +' is not mapped to checklist 'recurrent fever', because the table gives fever only and the methods mention patients with persistent fever. Table 2 'Inheritance' column 'AD' is the gene's inheritance mode, not the variant's origin, so inheritance = not reported. Zygosity comes from the group sentence 'Heterozygous genetic variants were found in the remaining 31 patients ... TNFAIP3'. No ACMG class is stated for the TNFAIP3 variant (Table 2 gnomAD 'No data', reference '-'). The transcript comes from Table 2's TNFAIP3 row, which prints the same c./p. as Table 3. The paper does not call this patient HA20; the diagnosis given is uAIDs, plus a formal sJIA diagnosis for all patients. No variants in other genes are listed for patient 26. Contradictions in the paper (none about patient 26's own data): Table 3 '+' counts differ from text/Table 1 for rash (28 vs 29), serositis (10 vs 'detected in 17 patients'), GI (5 vs 6) and eye (3 in Table 3/Table 1 vs 'Four patients (9%)' in the text); TREX1 is c.914A>G, p.Y305C in Table 2 but c.1079A>G, p.Y360C in Table 3 and the text; corticosteroids are 88% in the abstract vs 85% in the results; Pt 4 onset is 1.4 in Table 3 vs 1.5 years in the text. A script assembled the JSON from hand-chosen values; spans were checked verbatim by script.",
